<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>2.8.1: Understanding Inequality Symbols</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00496</md:content-id>
    <md:title>2.8.1: Understanding Inequality Symbols</md:title>
    <md:uuid>1d3b0476-ba7b-41cc-8928-bbee3f3fe412</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>For questions 1 – 3, match each inequality to the meaning of a symbol within it.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><title>Warm Up Activity</title><exercise data-content-id="5314b4a8-9916-43e2-8fe9-b836437b52a5" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\( h &gt; 50 \)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>less than or equal to</para><para>greater than</para><para>greater than or equal to</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! greater than</para><para>The correct answer is greater than. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="b5b31a3c-89b1-4e25-8348-ba7a045c2ced" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\( h \leq 20 \)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>less than or equal to</para><para>greater than</para><para>greater than or equal to</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! less than or equal to</para><para>The correct answer is less than or equal to .</para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="44ccedb4-59a0-4479-accf-337737c993a2" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\( 30 \geq h \)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>less than or equal to</para><para>greater than</para><para>greater than or equal to</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! greater than or equal to</para><para>The correct answer is greater than or equal to.</para></solution></exercise></section>
<!--Q#4-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> Is 25 a solution to any of the inequalities? Which one(s)? </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para>Yes; 25 is a solution to \(30 \geq h\) because 30 is greater than or equal to 25.</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Q#5-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> Is 40 a solution to any of the inequalities? Which one(s)? </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para>No; 40 is not a solution to any of the inequalities because 40 does not make any of the inequalities true when substituted in for \(h\).</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Q#6-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> Is 30 a solution to any of the inequalities? Which one(s)? </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para>Yes; 30 is a solution to \(30 \geq h\).</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
</section>
</content>
